==English==

===Etymnology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|silken|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|seolcen||made of silk, silken|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|silk|en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-silken.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Made of [[silk]].
# Having a [[smooth]], [[soft]], or [[light]] [[texture]], like that of silk; [[suggestive]] of silk.
#* '''1994''', [[w:Stephen Fry|Stephen Fry]], ''[[w:The Hippopotamus|The Hippopotamus]]'', ch. 2:
#*: He heard the '''silken''' rustle of a dressing-gown being drawn on.
# {{figuratively|of speech, singing, [[oratory]], etc.}} [[smooth|Smooth]]ly [[utter]]ed; [[flowing]], [[subtle]], or [[convincing]] in presentation.

